# The probability of the flip is the variable p, never assigned, so the bound is asked for
# every initial p; the flip is reached only where 0 <= p <= 1, where p is a probability, so no
# run reaches an out-of-range probability:
#   wp(S, c) = p * 1 + (1 - p) * 0 = p   for 0 <= p <= 1,   and 1 elsewhere (c := 1),
# so the upper bound 1 holds at every p.
# Expected: valid.  The twin of flip_state_above_one_upper_unknown.sgcl: an upper bound on a
# program whose probability is over program variables keeps its answer where that probability
# is in range.
c := 0;
if 0 <= p and p <= 1 {
	if flip(p) {
		c := 1
	}
} else {
	c := 1
}
return c
?Ex[c] <= 1
